TOS Priority-Inheritance Mutex

A kernel-managed mutex that prevents priority inversion.

When a high-priority thread blocks on a PI mutex held by a
low-priority thread, the holder is temporarily boosted to
the blocker's priority. This prevents medium-priority threads
from starving the high-priority thread (the classic priority
inversion bug that caused the Mars Pathfinder reset storm).

Unlike the basic mutex (which uses userspace atomics and
spin+yield), the PI mutex is fully managed by the kernel
so it can manipulate thread priorities and wait queues.

    module oskit

    pimutex_init(m: *PIMutex)
        pimutex_init_kernel(m)

    pimutex_lock(m: *PIMutex)
        val addr: i64 = i64(m)
        pimutex_lock_sys(addr)

    pimutex_unlock(m: *PIMutex)
        val addr: i64 = i64(m)
        pimutex_unlock_sys(addr)
